  {
   "id": 2,
   "ref": "616–620",
   "en": "driven from his borders, torn from Iulus's embrace, let him beg for help and watch his men die undeserved deaths; and even when he has surrendered to the terms of an unjust peace, let him not enjoy his kingdom, or the life he longed for, but let him fall before his time, and lie unburied in the middle of the sand.",
