  {
   "id": 3,
   "ref": "621–624",
   "en": "This I pray, these are the last words I pour out, with my own blood. And you, Tyrians — hunt down his line, his whole race to come, with your hatred, forever; send this as a gift to my ashes. Let there be no love between our peoples, no treaties, ever.",
   "en_marked": "[This|1] [I pray|2], [these|3] are the [last|5] [words|4] [I pour out|8], [with|6] {my own|Not in the Latin. Added to make clear it is Dido's own blood, since she is about to die.} [blood|7]. [And|9] [you|10], [Tyrians|12] — [hunt down|18] his [line|13], his [whole|16] [race|15] [to come|17], [with your hatred|19], {forever|Not in the Latin. Added to bring out the continuing force of exercete, keep harrying.}; [send|22] [this|21] as a [gift|24] [to|20] [my|23] [ashes|20]. [Let there be|30] [no|25] [love|26] [between our peoples|27], [no|28] [treaties|29], {ever|Added to bring out the solemn, lasting force of the future imperative sunto.}.",
